=== HINT 1: Allocate new region ===
BYTE *new_base = (BYTE*)VirtualAlloc(NULL, image_size,
    MEM_COMMIT | MEM_RESERVE, PAGE_EXECUTE_READWRITE);

=== HINT 2: Copy headers ===
memcpy(new_base, disk_img, headers_size);

=== HINT 3: Map sections ===
for (WORD i = 0; i < nt->FileHeader.NumberOfSections; i++) {
    if (sec[i].PointerToRawData == 0) continue;
    memcpy(new_base + sec[i].VirtualAddress,
           disk_img + sec[i].PointerToRawData,
           sec[i].SizeOfRawData);
}

=== HINT 4: Verify MZ magic ===
printf("MZ check: %c%c\n", new_base[0], new_base[1]);  // should be "MZ"

=== KEY INSIGHT ===
A complete reflective loader also needs:
  1. Base relocations: IMAGE_DIRECTORY_ENTRY_BASERELOC - patch absolute addresses
     if loaded at a different base than preferred (delta = new_base - preferred_base)
  2. Import resolution: walk IMAGE_IMPORT_DESCRIPTOR, call GetProcAddress for each
     imported function, write the IAT entry
  3. TLS callbacks: invoke IMAGE_DIRECTORY_ENTRY_TLS entries before entry point
  4. Entry point: cast to DllMain and call (DLL_PROCESS_ATTACH)
Popular open-source implementations: ReflectiveDLLInjection (Stephen Fewer),
  sRDI (shellcode reflective DLL injection - converts DLL to PIC shellcode).
